_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 4
---
order: 4
---
short_label: XI.4
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a straight line is set up at right angles to two straight lines which cut one another at their common point of section, then it is also at right angles to the plane passing through them.
----
proof:

For let a straight line {EF} be set up at right angles to the two straight lines {AB} and {CD} at {E}, the point at which the lines cut one another.

I say that {EF} is also at right angles to the plane passing through {AB} and {CD}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="320" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.4 diagram" src="propXI4.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // EF stands at E on the plane of AB and CD; the cut-offs AE = EB = CE =
    // ED, the random line GEH, the bases AD, CB and the six joins from F set
    // up three congruences (I.4, I.26, I.4/I.8) that end on the right angles
    // GEF and HEF, and XI.Def.3 carries that to the plane.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws AB, CD, AD and CB as the four edges of one crossed
    // quadrilateral ABCD (the green faces are the triangles AED and CEB), and
    // his joins AF..HF run from the far end to F. The walk needs AB and CD
    // before AD and CB are joined, and the joins drawn "from a point F", so
    // AB, CD, AD, CB and FA, FB, FC, FD, FG, FH are solid slide twins, hidden
    // at rest (initiallyHidden), as on IV.13. ABCD itself comes in with the
    // triangles AED, CEB; Joyce's AF..HF are never in a slide set.
    //
    // Everything else added is transparent: the half-lines AE, EB, CE, ED,
    // GE, EH, AG, BH; the triangles AED, CEB, AGE, BEH (explicit ;0 faces);
    // and refplane, a faceless polygon over baseplane for "the plane of
    // reference" (a plane element has no highlight stroke, and a face would
    // be raised over the figure, #140). Right angles are red squares (angleMarkerRight, drawn in the
    // projection): AEF, BEF, CEF, DEF by hypothesis, GEF and HEF once proved.
    // The markers at E are pinned (16 for squares, 20 for sectors) and shown
    // only on the slides that use them, so the eight at E do not ring out.
    // Angle and triangle names collide (AED, CEB, BEH): the triangles own
    // them, the angles take the display override.
    var BASE  = ["baseplane","A","B","C","D","E","F","EF","AB","CD"];
    var HYP   = BASE.concat(["rtAEF","rtCEF"]);
    var CUT   = BASE.concat(["AE","EB","CE","ED"]);
    var GEH   = CUT.concat(["G","H","GH","GE","EH"]);
    var JOIN  = GEH.concat(["AD","CB"]);
    var FIG   = JOIN.concat(["FA","FG","FD","FC","FH","FB"]);
    var VERT  = FIG.concat(["angAED","angCEB"]);
    var TRI   = FIG.concat(["ABCD","AED","CEB","angAED","angCEB"]);
    var BASEA = TRI.concat(["angDAE","angEBC"]);
    var FILL  = FIG.concat(["ABCD"]);
    var SMALL = FILL.concat(["angDAE","angEBC","angAEG","angBEH","AGE","BEH","AG","BH"]);
    var RT2   = FILL.concat(["rtAEF","rtBEF"]);
    var RT4   = RT2.concat(["rtCEF","rtDEF"]);
    var I8A   = FILL.concat(["angFAD","angFBC"]);
    var I4B   = I8A.concat(["AG","BH"]);
    var I8B   = FILL.concat(["angGEF","angHEF"]);
    var RIGHT = FILL.concat(["rtGEF","rtHEF"]);
    var PLANE = RIGHT.concat(["refplane"]);
    var DONE  = PLANE.concat(["rtAEF","rtCEF"]);
